That's very interesting, thanks for posting it. I wouldn't, however conclude
that this means knight and caveman are easiest and the wizard is most difficult.
I would expect knight and caveman to be more difficult than average and
that wizard to be easiest after the combat wombats. My caveman percentage
will soon be 33.3% (I don't see how this guy could fail) but it's only
because I didn't try a caveman until after a dozen ascensions covering
10 classes.
<p>I would conclude from these stats that a higher percentage of skilled,
previously ascended players play knights and cavemen, the newbies stick
to easier classes.
<p>The wizard has the most variety in starting equipment. I'm guessing
you're seeing less experienced players restarting games by quitting or
recklessly playing with fountains if they don't like their staring equipment.
<p>Another contributing factor could be that wizards are quite vulnerable
at first but catch up and surpass other classes somewhere around XL14.
For that matter, give me one wish and Magicbane and I'll bet I can ascend
that wizard.
